Project Explanation (Movie Ticket Booking System)

My project is a Movie Ticket Booking System, a web-based application designed to allow users to book movie tickets online easily and securely.

I developed the backend using Spring Boot, Spring Security, JWT, and MySQL, and I designed the system using a layered architecture with Controllers, Services, and Repositories.

🎯 Problem Statement

Traditional movie booking systems often face issues like:

Double booking of seats

Poor authentication security

No proper role-based access

Difficulty handling concurrent users

So the goal of my project was to build a secure and scalable booking system that:

Prevents seat conflicts

Supports role-based access (User & Theater Owner)

Handles secure authentication

Manages bookings and payments properly

🛠 Technologies Used

Backend: Spring Boot

Security: Spring Security + JWT (Access + Refresh Token)

Database: MySQL

ORM: JPA / Hibernate

Build Tool: Maven

Testing: Postman

👨‍💻 My Role & Responsibilities

I was responsible for:

Designing the complete database schema

Implementing authentication using JWT

Implementing refresh token rotation

Building role-based authorization

Designing booking logic with transaction handling

Implementing seat generation logic

Integrating payment flow

Sending email confirmation after successful booking

Handling global exception management

⭐ Key Features

1️⃣ JWT-Based Authentication

Access Token + Refresh Token

Refresh token stored securely

Logout invalidates refresh token

2️⃣ Role-Based Access Control

USER → Can book tickets, make payments, give feedback

THEATER_OWNER → Can create theaters, screens, and schedule shows

3️⃣ Automatic Seat Generation

When a screen is created, seats are auto-generated (Row-wise A1, A2… B1, B2…)

4️⃣ Concurrent Booking Protection

Uses transaction management

Prevents double booking of seats

5️⃣ Payment Integration Logic

Booking moves from PENDING → CONFIRMED after payment success

6️⃣ Feedback System

Only users who are logged in can add feedback

🚧 Biggest Challenge & Learning

The biggest challenge was handling concurrent seat booking.

If two users try to book the same seat at the same time, the system must prevent duplicate booking.

To solve this:

I used database transactions

Implemented proper locking mechanism

Ensured ACID properties

Handled seat availability validation before booking

This helped me deeply understand:

Transaction management

Isolation levels

Real-world concurrency problems

How large booking systems like BookMyShow work internally

